@startuml
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam ArrowColor #0b7a75
skinparam ComponentBorderColor #0b7a75
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #6b7280
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #f3f4f6
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9ca3af

skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #0b7a75
skinparam SequenceLifeLineBorderColor #9ca3af

title Opening one record: a click with no model in it, a live registry answer, and a write-back that cannot take away what only we know

actor "Person" as User
participant "Router\nop = provider-detail" as UR
participant "ProviderDetail tool" as Tool
participant "Detail route\n/provider-detail" as Route
participant "ProviderDetailService" as Svc
participant "NPPES\nlive query by NPI" as NPPES
database "Provider\ncollection" as DB
database "Session\npages.<page>.openNpi" as Session

User -> UR : click the record's link
note right of UR
  A click, not an utterance. No classifier and no model
  run on this path: the card already names the record, and
  everything shown is read from the record that NPI names.
end note

UR -> Session : this page is showing this record
note right of Session
  Recorded on the page the record belongs to — facility
  when entity_type is "2", care giver otherwise. Writing
  every open record to the care-giver page meant nothing
  could take a facility down when the person moved on.

  openNpi is written here and is not one of the parameters
  the record declares. openNctId, its trial equivalent, is.
end note

UR -> Tool : Request(npi, entity_type, card fields)
Tool -> Route : POST /provider-detail
activate Route
Route -> Svc : lookup(npi, entity_type)
activate Svc

alt the facility page opened it
  Svc -> NPPES : query by NPI
  NPPES --> Svc : entity type
  note right of Svc
    Checked against the live answer, not the stored record,
    because the stored record is the thing that would be
    wrong. Not an organization means the person is told no
    facility was found.
  end note
end

Svc -> NPPES : query by NPI
activate NPPES
NPPES --> Svc : live record, or nothing
deactivate NPPES

alt the registry did not answer
  Svc -> DB : read the stored record
  DB --> Svc : record as we hold it
  note right of Svc
    Shown as we hold it, with no comparison. Not answering
    leaves us no reason to doubt the record; answering with
    something different is what gives us one.
  end note
else the registry answered
  Svc -> DB : read the stored record
  DB --> Svc : record
  Svc -> Svc : project both onto the fields\nthe registry owns, and compare\nname, addresses, taxonomies,\nother identifiers, status, enumeration date
  note right of Svc
    Projected onto what the registry owns rather than
    stripped of the fields somebody remembered to name.
    Naming the exclusions meant our address — carrying a
    county and spelled-out labels the registry has never
    heard of — could never equal the live one, so every
    record diverged the first time it was opened.
  end note

  alt something diverged
    Svc -> Svc : merge: start from OUR record,\napply only the registry's fields
    note right of Svc
      Our address is carried forward whole and the registry's
      eight fields are applied onto it. Building the new
      address from the live one and copying back a named
      field is what silently dropped everything else, and it
      would drop the next enrichment added the same way.

      Only the primary practice address and the mailing
      address are touched. The live answer does not describe
      secondary practice locations, so emitting only what it
      named deleted the rest for every provider holding more
      than one.

      Taxonomy flags are preserved when the taxonomies
      change: the catalogue may be unreachable, and a
      recompute that cannot run must not blank them.

      An address we have never seen has nothing to carry
      forward, so that one is geocoded for its county.
    end note

    Svc -> Svc : compare the merged record to the stored one,\nprovenance left out of the comparison

    alt the merge changed something real
      Svc -> DB : replace the record
      Svc -> DB : read it back
      DB --> Svc : the record as now stored
    else the merge changed nothing
      note right of Svc
        Not written. Provenance is stamped unconditionally,
        so comparing the whole document would differ every
        time and say nothing about whether anything changed.
        Without this, a record whose county the geocoder
        cannot answer is rewritten every time it is looked at.
      end note
    end
  end
end

Svc --> Route : the panel's projection
deactivate Svc

alt the embedding text changed
  Route -> Route : schedule the re-embed to run\nafter the response has gone
  note right of Route
    Scheduled rather than awaited: the person is waiting for
    a panel, and the vector matters to the next search
    rather than to this one.
  end note
end

Route --> Tool : detail
deactivate Route
Tool --> UR : detail
UR --> User : the record as the registry reports it now

@enduml
